intro:
The orthogonal Procrustes problem is a matrix approximation problem in linear algebra.  In its classical form, one is given two matrices 



        A


    {\displaystyle A}

 and 



        B


    {\displaystyle B}

 and asked to find an orthogonal matrix 



        Ω


    {\displaystyle \Omega }

 which most closely maps 



        A


    {\displaystyle A}

 to 



        B


    {\displaystyle B}

.
